window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"volibear","b":"locke","win":["Volibear","Volibear","Volibear","Volibear","Skill","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Thundering Smash's speed and stun runs down his short range, W Frenzied Maul heals you through his chip, and his own W Soul Ignition helps you win the HP race - bully every wave."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"The lane turns honest: R Purgatory's threshold math preys on your big health bar, so stop coin-flip all-ins - engage off your Q stun with E shield up, and back out if his totem is waiting."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His first AP item is the danger spike - W Soul Ignition burst plus a saved execute totem can delete even your health pool, so track his R before every commit."},{"when":"Late","text":"Skill era: your W heal can outpace the totem if timed after its damage, but a mistimed engage into a held Purgatory is a scripted death."}],"wants":{"you":["Q stun engages before his E reset is up","Frenzied Maul second bites to out-heal his chip","His R totem dodged or baited before you dive"],"foe":["Chip damage stacking toward totem threshold","E Ashen Pursuit resets to dodge your Q stun","R Purgatory dropped mid-fight when your W is down"]},"early":"Locke can't keep up with you before level 6. Ritual Nails (10s) marks you from 950, but Locke's attacks have to reach you to cash in the marks, and Thundering Smash stuns him first. Soul Ignition (18s) makes him faster, but it burns his own health, which your Frenzied Maul second bite out-heals. Ashen Pursuit (10s) is his only dash, so charge Q after he's used it. Silver Stake adds damage as your health drops, so trade from high health. At 6 it's even: Purgatory (120s) can execute you, so don't dive him low.","mid":"At 6 the matchup becomes a math problem: your huge health bar is exactly what R Purgatory's threshold loves, so the totem can turn your winning all-in into an execution. It stays a skill fight - engage with E Sky Splitter's shield, hold W's heal for after his burst, and disengage the second his totem drops.","late":"His first item is genuinely dangerous - burst plus execute deletes health bars your W cannot rebuild in time - and late game settles into a timing war: if you land Stormbringer's dive and your W heal after his totem's damage, you win; if he holds Purgatory for your commit, you die on schedule.","whys":["Q Thundering Smash's stun and W healing let you bully his short level-1 range.","Your sustain and The Relentless Storm autos out-trade him at 2.","Frenzied Maul's second-bite healing owns the level-3 all-in.","You stay ahead on raw health and heals through levels 4-5.","At 6 it turns even - Purgatory's threshold preys on your big health bar, but timed W heals can outpace the totem.","His first-item burst plus a saved execute totem lets him delete you.","Late comes down to skill - whether he times the totem past your W heal."]});
