window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"volibear","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Volibear","Volibear","Skill","Skill","Volibear","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Thundering Smash's speed and stun arrives and he cannot escape your commits: run him down, W-mark him, and cash the chase-and-heal loop before his mid-lane spike."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"His Q double-slash with the knock-up recast and his E dash-slice start punishing your engage windows - engage off a landed stun only."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Coin-flip ultimates: Stormbringer's dive and health versus his R damage-and-heal - whoever forces the other to burn their answer first takes the fight."},{"when":"2 items","text":"His reset Q poke and empowered E now out-rotate you and his R out-heals your drain - stop dueling and use your engage for your team instead."}],"wants":{"you":["Q stun engages he cannot walk away from","W Frenzied Maul loops on a marked target","Stormbringer dives before his R is ready"],"foe":["Q double-slash, then the knock-up recast","E Golden Onslaught punishes on your whiffed stun","The two-item era where his rotation wins"]},"early":"Level 1 is even: The Darkin Glaive (10s) slashes twice and heals Zaahen, and your autos trade back. Levels 2 and 3 are yours, because Thundering Smash stuns him before he can recast Q for the knock-up. Frenzied Maul's second bite heals you more than his Q heals him. Dreaded Return (14s) pulls you in from 850, so sidestep its line. At levels 4-5 it's even, as Aureate Rush (10s) dashes and slices around you. At 6 it stays even: Grim Deliverance heals him, and Cultivation of War stacks give him extra AD.","mid":"Levels 4-5 drift back to even as his Q double-slash and E dash-slice (10s at rank 1) punish sloppy engage attempts, so commit only off a landed stun. Level 6 is a genuine coin-flip - your Stormbringer dive against his R damage-and-heal - and the winner is whoever baits the other ultimate first.","late":"Your first item keeps you the stronger all-in bruiser and that is your last great dueling era, because two items in he takes over: reset Q poke and empowered E outpace your rotation and his R sustain out-heals your W drain - late, spend Stormbringer as a teamfight opener, not a 1v1 gamble.","whys":["Level 1 is even farm before your Q ramp and stun come online.","Level 2 is yours: Thundering Smash's speed and stun commit trades he cannot escape.","Level 3 stays yours - the full Q-W chase-and-heal loop wins extended trades.","Levels 4-5 level back to even as his Q poke and E burst punish your engage windows.","Level 6 is a coin-flip - your Stormbringer dive against his R damage-and-heal all-in.","On your first item your chase and W sustain make you the stronger all-in bruiser.","Two items in he takes over - Q resets and empowered E outpace your rotation and his R sustain out-heals your drain."]});
